Usage: locale [OPTION]

Get locale-specific information.
Write locale-specific information to standard output.

OPTIONS:
  -a, --all            print all available locales
  -c, --category-name  print the names of defined locale categories
  -k, --keyword-name   print the names and values of keyword definitions
  -m, --charmaps       print available character maps
  -v, --verbose        print more information
                       print locale information
      --help           display this help and exit
  -V, --version        output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
